The attached image illustrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and increases antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest CD86 expression among OVA-positive myeloid cells in the draining lymph node, a key costimulatory molecule for T cell activation. Panel B further phenotypes OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs, suggesting Nano-11 preferentially targets antigen to CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells. Panel C demonstrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide (AH), effectively retains antigen at the injection site for several days post-injection, whereas soluble OVA dissipates rapidly, thereby prolonging antigen availability for immune cell uptake and activation.